# Trivy misconfiguration findings accepted for this stack, with reasons.
# The stack is a short-lived demo (created and destroyed in about an hour)
# and is built to cost about $0. Revisit these before running it long term.

# CloudFront access logging: needs a log bucket and adds storage, for a demo
# with nothing to audit.
AWS-0010

# AWS WAF: billed monthly per web ACL and per rule even when idle. Media URLs
# are unguessable UUIDs and the budget alert covers abuse during a demo.
AWS-0011

# S3 server access logging: same reasoning as CloudFront logging.
AWS-0089

# S3 versioning: demo media is disposable (7-day expiry, force_destroy), and
# old versions would only add storage cost.
AWS-0090

# Customer-managed KMS key: about $1/month per key plus request fees. Objects
# are still encrypted at rest with SSE-S3.
AWS-0132
